{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 124, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual input-to-output path where none existed yields far larger gains than replacing an existing op on edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Creating a missing direct input-to-output path is much more valuable than swapping an existing edge-3 op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the residual skip on edge 3 with a conv removes the identity shortcut and hurts accuracy."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 0 when edge 1 is already absent disconnects node 2 from the input and collapses the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node 1 is dead, a conv on edge 5 supplies the depth the cell otherwise lacks."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pool on the first edge with a learnable conv gives the biggest improvement."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Gains from a 3x3 conv on edge 1 are smaller when the edge was absent than when it replaces skip or pool."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "If node 1 holds only pooled input, adding a conv on edge 4 contributes more needed learnable capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding any path from node 2 to the output beats replacing an existing conv or s